the missing glyph trace covered the wrong range

The threshold was characters above 0x2000, chosen when the question was the Command symbol at
U+2318. Greek, Cyrillic and Arabic all sit BELOW it, so the one instrument that could have named
this printed nothing for exactly the case it was needed for. Any character above ASCII now, and
sixty lines rather than four.

WHAT IT SAID IMMEDIATELY, for the Money Manager EX language list (#216):

  CIDER_NOGLYPH u+0644 face=TeX Gyre Heros style=Regular     Arabic lam
  CIDER_NOGLYPH u+043b face=TeX Gyre Heros style=Regular     Cyrillic el
  CIDER_NOGLYPH u+0430 face=TeX Gyre Heros style=Regular     Cyrillic a

The UI font resolves to TeX Gyre Heros, a Helvetica clone with Latin and basic Greek and NO Cyrillic
and NO Arabic, which is the whole of the symptom: an Arabic or Cyrillic name draws as nothing, and
accented Greek drops mid word while unaccented Greek survives.
